924"] ", the three-day event has always consisted of a day each of cross-country, dressage, and jumping. The 1920 format, however, was also used at the 1919 Inter-Allied Games in Paris. That competition had been won by the French rider Major Joseph de Soras, who, for some reason, was not entered at Antwerp. The sixth-place finisher at Antwerp, " [:a {:href "/athletes/11743"} "Harry Chamberlin"] " (USA), had finished second at the Inter-Allied Games after leading through the first two days."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12476"} "Helmer, Greve Mörner"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/990"} "Geria"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1,775.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12343"} "Åge Lundström"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2717"} "Yrsa"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "1,738.75"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11705"} "Ettore Caffaratti"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/382"} "Caniche"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "1,733.75"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td 